Automate Doc Generation with AI and Templates
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will:

Design a template-driven documentation pipeline combining Markdown templates, shell scripting, and local AI generation
Integrate Ollama (local LLM) into an automated content-generation workflow
Build a config-driven variable substitution system for document metadata
Implement automated linting and quality gates in a documentation pipeline
Produce a maintainer-facing runbook for the automation system
Manage the pipeline as a versioned, reproducible artifact in Git
Prerequisites
Strong Linux CLI proficiency (bash scripting, process substitution, piping, sed/awk)
Working knowledge of Git (branching, commits, .gitignore)
Familiarity with Markdown syntax and YAML/INI config formats
Basic exposure to LLM prompting concepts (system/user prompts, context windows)
Comfort installing and troubleshooting packages independently
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Linux machine (Ubuntu) via Start Lab.

